    "lawCode": "Add §344-k, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3220\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system in Oneida county as the \"Kevin F. Crossley\nMemorial Highway\"\n\n \nTITLE:\n\nAN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system in Oneida County as the \"Kevin F.  Crossley\nMemorial Highway\".\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nDesignates a portion of state route 69 (Oriskany Boulevard) in the\nVillage of Whitesboro as the Kevin F. Crossley Memorial Highway.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends the highway law by adding a new section 344-k designating a\nportion of state route 69, Oriskany Boulevard, in the Village of Whites-\nboro, as the \"Kevin F. Crossley Memorial Highway\".\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nKevin F. Crossley was a dedicated and beloved Police Officer in the\nVillage of Whitesboro who on April 11, 2018, tragically lost his life\nwhile on duty protecting the community.\n\nThe Village of Whitesboro has requested this designation as a way to\nrecognize and honor the sacrifice made by Officer Crossley, a seven-year\nveteran of the Police Department and a life long village resident.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018 - S. 8621 Passed Senate/A. 10748 Transportation Committee.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n30 days.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
